/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  A COLUMN THAT STARTS FROM THE INTERIOR THE CASE DECLARES.

  Physically this is column01 -- benzene/toluene, Raoult, 15 stages, feed on
  8, R = 2, D = 50 kmol/h -- and the answer is the same answer.  What differs
  is where the ITERATION STARTS, and that is the whole subject of the case.

  THE OPENFOAM READING OF A STATE DIRECTORY.  In OpenFOAM a time directory
  holds one file per FIELD, and that file carries `boundaryField` AND
  `internalField` together: the conditions at the edges of the domain and the
  values inside it, in one place, so the directory is a COMPLETE, RESTARTABLE
  snapshot.  Choupo`s `0/` used to carry only the boundary half -- one file
  per STREAM -- while what each unit held inside it existed nowhere a case
  could declare it.  Since 2026-09-06 a state view carries both:

      0/<stream>                       a FILE is a stream   (the boundary)
      0/<SECTOR>/<unit>/<kind>         a DIRECTORY is a unit`s interior

  This case declares `0/column16/stageProfile`: the temperature and the
  liquid and vapour compositions on all 15 stages, in exactly the grammar the
  run writes to `converged/column16/stageProfile`.  The same object travels
  both ways, which is what makes the snapshot restartable -- run the case,
  copy the file from `converged/` to `0/`, and the next run starts where the
  last one finished.

  WHY IT MATTERS HERE, and it is not the speed.  Until this slice the column
  seeded its own interior in CODE -- "initial T-profile (linear between
  guesses)" -- undeclared, unseen and unowned, which is exactly the silent
  crutch Choupo forbids for every other solver aid (every aid is explicit in a
  dict and announces itself when it binds).  Now the unit says which of the
  two routes it took, on every run, both ways:

      [seed] interior read from 0/ (stageProfile): 15 stages, T ... K
      [seed] interior seeded by the unit: linear T between the guesses ...

  A DECLARED PROFILE THAT DOES NOT SATISFY THE BALANCES IS A SEED, NOT AN
  ANSWER.  Nothing checks this file against the column equations -- the
  iteration does that, and it moves off any profile that is wrong.  Edit a
  stage temperature by fifty kelvin and the column still converges to the same
  distillate; it simply takes more outer iterations to get there.  What IS
  checked is that the declaration describes THIS column: the stage count, the
  component set, and that every number is a number.  A mismatch REFUSES by
  name and names the remedy -- a seed silently ignored would be the silence
  this case exists to end.

  WHAT THE STUDENT SHOULD DO WITH IT.  Run the case and read the `iterations`
  KPI; then delete `0/column16/` and run it again.  Both runs reach the same
  column; only one of them had to search for it.  That difference is the
  entire value of a restartable snapshot, and it is why an interior is STATE
  and not a report.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only
// -- and, since 2026-09-06, the INTERIOR of each unit in 0/<unit>/<kind>.

units
(
    {
        name        column16;
        type        distillationColumn;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( distillate  bottoms );

        operation
        {
            nStages        15;
            feedStage      8;
            refluxRatio    2.0;
            distillateRate 50.0 kmol/h;
            feedQuality    1.0;
            P              1.01325 bar;
        }

        compositionTol   1e-7;
        maxOuterIter     200;
    }
);
